  "title": "D-reviewhint finish (T-1585 lineage): fix the NameError and UnboundLocalError in review_packet and update the two tests that pinned the 8000-char bound",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, plan label D-reviewhint-finish. Finishes T-1585 (held gate_red since 2026-10-02 22:32). Fresh task, not a resumed fix round: the Planner created your branch task/THIS-TASK at e891d81 (the head of task/T-1585, which holds the whole D-reviewhint change). Keep everything already committed.\n\nThe original spec of T-1585 (read it with bus.get('T-1585')['spec'] or in .orchestrator/tasks/T-1585.json) still applies: (a) the review packet's expand hint is the same git diff -U3 base...HEAD command scoped_diff runs, via one shared base helper; (b) the diff budget is max(1, [limits].review_diff_chars, default 12000) with no 8000 constant; (c) the packet's base line is the merge-base short sha and it names the branch under review.\n\nGate failures on e891d81 (tests/test_spawn.py, full suite):\n- ERROR test_bounded_diff_expansion_hint: NameError: name 'reviewed' is not defined (a variable used in the review packet code before it is assigned or under a wrong name).\n- ERROR test_render_does_not_rebound_diff: UnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'task' (a local named task is read before assignment in the changed code path).\n- FAIL test_review_packet_single_bounding_pass_no_nested_truncation: 15310 not less than or equal to 8200; FAIL test_review_prompt_diff_is_bounded: 0 != 1. These two old tests pin the removed 8000-char bound. Change (b) intentionally removes it, so update them to set [limits].review_diff_chars explicitly (for example 8000) in their config and keep asserting single-pass bounding and exactly one truncation marker at that configured size; do not weaken them otherwise.\n\nFix the two code errors in orchestrator/spawn.py (read the tracebacks by running the two tests), keep both acceptance tests of T-1585 passing, and touch nothing else. Commit first, then run tests/test_spawn.py in the foreground, then the whole tests directory once with the command .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh uses; report failures only. Never background a command.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1585"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_review_packet_hint_names_base_range_and_branch: passes: for a task whose worktree has one commit beyond goal/<parent>, review_packet's expand hint is exactly the scoped_diff command with the goal base (`git -C <wt> diff -U3 goal/<parent>...HEAD -- <scope>`), the packet's base line shows the merge-base short sha (not HEAD), and the packet names the branch under review (task['branch'] when set, else task/<id>) with the HEAD short sha; with no goal branch the hint and base use origin/main",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_review_packet_diff_budget_honours_review_diff_chars: passes: with [limits].review_diff_chars 20000 and a scoped diff of 15000 chars, the packet contains the whole diff and no 'more lines' marker; with review_diff_chars 3000 the diff section is cut with the marker and the hint from the first test; the packet never cuts the diff at 8000 when the configured value is larger",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
